hexagon: call the int16 activation evaluators from the op entry points

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus the patches before this one in patches/series.

Files:
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/hvx-act-i16.h  the switch that selects the path
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/unary-ops.c    SIGMOID and SILU
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/act-ops.c      SWIGLU

The problem

The patch before this one adds the int16 evaluators, and nothing calls them. SIGMOID, SILU and
SWIGLU still take the qfloat chain of about 25 dependent steps, and SILU and SWIGLU walk the
row twice: once for the sigmoid and once for the multiply.

The change

Each of the three op entry points takes the int16 path when htp_act_i16_mode is not 0, which is
the default. The SILU and the SWIGLU forms also become one pass, thus each row is read and
written one time instead of two.

Measured in tools/htp-lab against a float64 reference, cycles for each vector of a 9216 row:

    sigmoid   49.57 -> 22.79   2.18 times faster
    silu      57.52 -> 20.54   2.80 times faster
    swiglu    58.60 -> 23.06   2.54 times faster

The error

The int16 path is not exact. Its NMSE is 1.5e-10 to 2.5e-9 against a baseline whose NMSE is
5e-15 to 7e-15, and its largest absolute error is 1.1e-4 for the sigmoid, 1.6e-4 for the SILU
and 3.1e-4 for the SWIGLU. The f16 rounding of the input is the whole of that error, not the
polynomial and not the output step. The gated delta net of this backend already accepts 3.0e-07
of NMSE, thus these values are inside what the tests permit, but they are a regression from an
exact baseline and a reviewer must see them. HTP_ACT_I16_MODE 0 takes the old path back.

The two other GLU forms, swiglu_oai and swiglu_clamp, keep the old path. Their formulas differ
and no measurement of them against the reference exists.

diff -urN a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/act-ops.c b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/act-ops.c
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/act-ops.c	2026-09-20 03:57:04.346995302 +0300
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/act-ops.c	2026-09-20 03:57:04.367713920 +0300
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #include <math.h>
 #include <string.h>
 
+#include "hvx-act-i16.h"
 #include "hex-dma.h"
 #include "hvx-utils.h"
 
@@ -145,8 +146,13 @@
         const uint8_t * restrict src1_ptr = (const uint8_t *) src1 + (ib * src1_row_size_aligned);
         uint8_t * restrict dst_ptr        = (uint8_t *) dst + (ib * dst_row_size_aligned);
 
-        hvx_sigmoid_f32_aa(dst_ptr, src0_ptr, nc);
-        hvx_mul_mul_f32_aa(dst_ptr, src0_ptr, dst_ptr, src1_ptr, nc);
+        // One pass gives the SwiGLU. The two-pass form reads and writes the row twice.
+        if (htp_act_i16_mode) {
+            hvx_swiglu_i16_f32_aa(dst_ptr, src0_ptr, src1_ptr, nc);
+        } else {
+            hvx_sigmoid_f32_aa(dst_ptr, src0_ptr, nc);
+            hvx_mul_mul_f32_aa(dst_ptr, src0_ptr, dst_ptr, src1_ptr, nc);
+        }
     }
 }
 
diff -urN a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/hvx-act-i16.h b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/hvx-act-i16.h
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/hvx-act-i16.h	2026-09-20 03:57:04.341132073 +0300
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/hvx-act-i16.h	2026-09-20 03:57:04.367156403 +0300
@@ -42,6 +42,15 @@
 
 #include "hvx-base.h"
 
+// Which path the op entry points take. 1 is the int16 evaluator of this file, 0 is the qfloat
+// chain that came before it. The int16 path is 2.2 to 2.8 times faster, and its error is the
+// f16 rounding of the input: NMSE 1.5e-10 to 2.5e-9, at most 3.1e-4 of absolute error, against
+// a baseline that was exact to f32. Set this to 0 to take the old path back.
+#ifndef HTP_ACT_I16_MODE
+#define HTP_ACT_I16_MODE 1
+#endif
+static int htp_act_i16_mode = HTP_ACT_I16_MODE;
+
 #define HVX_ACT_I16_DEGREE 4
 #define HVX_ACT_I16_SCALE  16
 #define HVX_ACT_I16_EBASE  3
